;; Splint — idiom / anti-pattern linting for Gates of Truth.
;;
;; Read by the `:splint` alias (see deps.edn) and by bin/analyze.
;;
;; POLICY: no rule is disabled globally. Splint ships with sensible defaults and
;; a blanket `{:enabled false}` here would silently exempt every future site of
;; that rule — which is precisely the failure mode
;; kanban/tasks/static-analysis-regression-2026-07-24.md exists to stop.
;;
;; Suppressions are PER-FORM and carry their reason at the site:
;;
;;   ;; Intentional: <why this rule is wrong here>
;;   #_{:splint/disable [lint/catch-throwable]}
;;   (defn ...)
;;
;; A form-level marker covers findings nested anywhere inside that form, so one
;; marker on a `defn` suffices for several sites in its body. Note that ns-level
;; `{:splint/disable [...]}` metadata is NOT honoured by splint 1.24.0 — verified
;; 2026-07-25; do not reach for it.
;;
;; The suppressions live at:
;;   src/infra/dev/window/loop.clj      lint/catch-throwable ×8 (render-loop
;;                                      guards; rationale in the ns docstring)
;;   src/domain/ecs/tick.clj            lint/catch-throwable (worker future must
;;                                      always .put or the fold deadlocks)
;;   src/domain/em/lorentz.clj          lint/let-if (bound value is a never-read
;;                                      boolean naming a physics gate)
;;   src/domain/stellar/classifier/state.clj
;;                                      lint/identical-branches (two independent
;;                                      physical criteria for stardom)
;;   src/domain/narrowing.clj           naming/conversion-functions (false
;;                                      positive on a predicate)
;;   src/infra/render/hud.clj           style/apply-str ×2 (char-seq repeat)
;;   test/domain/narrative_test.clj     style/eq-zero (nil-safe, stronger)
;;   test/domain/physics/cache_test.clj style/eq-zero ×3 (ditto)
;;
;; If you add a suppression, add it to that list. If you find one that no longer
;; applies, delete the marker rather than leaving it as cover.
{}
